    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key to `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `util/IdentityKeys.java`:\n- `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` \u2192 lower-case 64-char hex SHA-256 over the three `|`-joined segments (null telephone/email \u2192 empty segment).\n- `soundex(name)` \u2192 a standard American Soundex implementation (first letter + up to three code digits, zero-padded; vowels separate same-coded consonants, h/w are transparent). Both are `static` so the controller and mapper compute the key identically.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.identityKey(owner)`** now delegates to `IdentityKeys` \u2014 so the exposed DTO `identityKey` field is the 64-hex-char key (satisfies `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1`**:\n- `identityKey(owner)` delegates to `IdentityKeys` (used by the single `rejectDuplicateIdentity` 409 check, still filtering out `deleted` owners, still after `normalizeEmail`'s domain blocklist).\n- `findPossibleDuplicate(owner)` now soft-matches when the **identityKey differs** but **soundex(lastName) and postcode match** (was: same lastName + postcode + different telephone). Because telephone now feeds the key, two owners with the same lastName+postcode but different telephones get different keys \u2014 no longer a 409, instead flagged as a soft match.\n\n`householdId` is retained (still used by the mapper for membership-level capping / household points); it was simply dropped from the identity key. Javadocs were updated to match the new behaviour.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
